  {
    "description": "Initialise a new HyperFrames project. Writes index.html using the chosen Tailwind-first template and returns it, ready to fill. Available templates: neon-launch (Dark purple/pink, 1920x1080, 18s - dramatic product launch) | social-reel (Bold vertical, 1080x1920, 15s - punchy social promo) | clean-minimal (Light editorial, 1920x1080, 15s - typography-forward) | tech-data (Dark/teal, 1920x1080, 20s - metrics and product proof) | warm-cinema (Amber/gold, 1920x1080, 18s - cinematic storytelling) | scaffold-social-reel (Structural scaffold: 1080x1920, 15s, 6 scenes, 1 shader group) | scaffold-launch-teaser (Structural scaffold: 1920x1080, 25s, 8 scenes, 2 shader groups) | scaffold-explainer (Structural scaffold: 1920x1080, 45s, 12 scenes, 2 shader groups) | scaffold-cinematic (Structural scaffold: 1920x1080, 60s, 7 scenes, 2 shader groups, long durations). Use force: true to overwrite an existing project.",
    "name": "hyperframes_init",
    "parameters": {
      "properties": {
        "design_path": {
          "description": "A design spec already in Files (the user's design.md, DESIGN.md or frame.md): copied into the project, its tokens theme the scaffold. With frame_preset too, the preset directs the composition and this design.md holds the brand.",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "force": {
          "description": "Overwrite if the project already exists (default: false)",
          "type": "boolean",
        },
        "frame_preset": {
          "description": "A HyperFrames design preset to direct the composition: saved as the project's frame.md (brand tokens + frame treatments + Do/Don't) and used to theme the scaffold. Options: biennale-yellow (warm parchment, solar-yellow blooms, indigo ink, Instrument Serif display, 1px hairlines; for confident, atmospheric, museum-catalogue elegance) | blockframe (maximalist neobrutalist: thick black borders, hard offset shadows, candy pastels; for bold, punchy, playful-loud) | blue-professional (corporate cream with one cobalt accent, Space Grotesk + Inter, soft tinted cards; for measured, executive, investment-research rigor) | bold-poster (tilted Shrikhand display, tomato red on cream, Libre Baskerville body, double-border grids; for printed, powerful, vintage editorial gravitas) | broadside (industrial newsprint poster: ink and fire-orange, massive lowercase Barlow 900; for bold, typographic, declarative) | capsule (every container a pill, cream paper, candy palette, Bodoni Moda headlines; for friendly, soft, warm editorial) | cartesian (sparse museum catalog: warm stone, Playfair Display, taupe hairline grid; for quiet authority, literary restraint) | cobalt-grid (two-color risograph: cream paper, cobalt ink graph grid, Newsreader + Hanken Grotesk; for systemic, editorial clarity) | code-editorial (warm cream brand book, terracotta coral accent, EB Garamond, navy code surface; for developer launches, code changes, docs with editorial calm) | coral (coral, ink and cream at hard edges, Bebas Neue caps, diagonal hatch, giant numerals; for graphic, structuralist magazine confidence) | creative-mode (neo-brutalist cream, 4px ink borders, Archivo Black caps, JetBrains Mono data; for sparse but punchy, geometric presence) | daisy-days (sunny-garden pastels, charcoal outlines, hard shadows, Fredoka One + Quicksand, doodles; for playful, childlike, sticker-sheet warmth) | editorial-forest (green, pink and cream triad, Source Serif 4 display, JetBrains Mono chrome; for spacious, literary, quiet confidence).",
          "enum": [
